<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the two Quick Look .appex bundles (S58-e / S59).

  macOS REQUIRES an app extension to be sandboxed: PlugInKit (pkd) will not register or launch an
  extension whose code signature carries no com.apple.security.app-sandbox entitlement. Signing the
  bundle with no entitlement dictionary at all -- which is what make-dmg.sh did before this file
  existed -- therefore produces extensions that are structurally perfect and never load, while the
  Quick Look agent keeps retrying them. That is the leading suspect for the Finder stalls reported
  against the DMG.

  files.user-selected.read-only is the access a Quick Look provider needs: the system hands it one
  file URL at a time, and a sandboxed extension cannot read even that without it.

  ⚠ UNVERIFIED ON HARDWARE. There is no Mac in this project's loop; this is a documented platform
  requirement that was demonstrably not being met, not a fix confirmed against the symptom. The
  triage commands in README.md are how to tell.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-only</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
